        ____________________________________________________
        Installing "Nicholson London Pages" on your Psion 3a
        ____________________________________________________

This product contains "Nicholson London Pages", bringing you up-to-date
information on over 3,100 venues and services in London.  You can copy 
any combination of the four supplied databases to your Psion, in order
to meet your personal requirements.   

The databases are licensed for a period of 30 days, after which, you
will need to register them to continue having access.  During this
period, a 'nag screen' is displayed on entering and exiting the
databases and after every fourth database search.  This nag screen and 
the 30 day limit are both removed on registration.

A single copy of "Pages Viewer" software, requiring approximately 100kb,
is used to access any number of Mobile Pages databases.  Pages Viewer
is available as MP_VIEW.ZIP from www.mobilepages.com and from the 
CompuServe Palmtop A Forum and from the CIX mobile_pages conference.
Comprehensive HELP on using this product is available by pressing the
HELP key once you have entered Pages Viewer.  Additional HELP is
available as a Word 6.0 document in the file MP_HELP.  This files
is available at the same locations as mp_view.zip.

Database name					Size	    Code
-------------                                   ----        ----
Accommodation & entertainment		       	128kb	    nga
Shopping & consumer services			 99kb       ngb
Information, sport & health			109kb	    ngc
Sightseeing, leisure & children’s London	114kb	    ngd

1. INSTALLATION INSTRUCTIONS
____________________________

   THREE METHODS OF LOADING THESE DATABASES AND PAGES VIEWER 
   SOFTWARE ARE AVAILABLE AND ARE DOCUMENTED BELOW: 

     GO TO SECTION A TO LOAD USING PSIWIN
     GO TO SECTION B TO LOAD USING THE CYCLONE DISK DRIVE
     GO TO SECTION C TO LOAD USING MCLINK/RCOM

   ALTERNATIVELY, if you are familiar with copying files, then simply
   unzip mp_view.zip and mp_londn.zip, restoring the original directory
   structure (eg pkunzip -d <filename>).  Copy all files in \app and
   \app\pages directories to the same directories on any device on
   your Psion and use Psion-i to install the 2 applications.

   A) Installation using PSIWIN
   ____________________________
     Ensure ‘conversion’ is disabled.  You can check this in Psion Manager
     by selecting "conversions" from the "setup" menu and ensuring the
     "allow convert on Drag & Drop" box is clear, ie not selected.  Connect
     the Psion 3Link serial cable between the PC and your Psion 3a.  On the
     Psion, from the System screen, use Psion-l to set 'Remote link'  to 
     'On' and ensure the 'Baud rate' is set correctly.

     · Create the \app\pages directory on your Psion, if it doesn’t exist. 
       Copy the files in the \app directory to a \app directory on any 
       device on your Psion 3a and then copy all files in the \app\pages
       directory that start with the 3 characters 'mp_' and with ‘ng&’,
       to a \app\pages directory on your Psion.

     · For each database you want to copy to your Psion, copy all files 
       beginning with its 3 letter database code, (eg nga ... see above) 
       from the \app\pages directory on the diskette, to a \app\pages
       directory on any device on your Psion.
        
     · Use Psion-i to install the PAGESmgr and PAGESi icons on the System
       screen.  If this is the first time you have loaded Mobile Pages,
       simply press ‘Enter’ on the PAGESi icon.  This will allow you to
       access, search and view the database(s) you have just downloaded.
       (If, when you select PAGESi, you receive the message ‘Use PAGESmgr
       to load software’, you have not successfully copied the required 
       files to \app\pages, as documented above.  Return to the previous
       step!).  If  you have loaded a new version of software or 
       additional databases, enter PAGESmgr and select ‘Auto install’,
       before entering PAGESi.
 

   B) Installation using the CYCLONE diskette drive
   ________________________________________________ 
    Insert the Mobile Pages diskette into the Cyclone and plug the Cyclone
    into the Psion. Use Psion-i to install PAGESmgr from drive c: and enter
    PAGESmgr.

    · Select ‘Software copy/download’, followed by ‘Copy between Psion
      devices’.  Copy from C, to the device of your choice.
    · Select ‘Database copy/download’, followed by ‘Copy between Psion devices’.
      Then, for each database you want to copy, supply its 3 character code,
      and copy it from device C, to the device of your choice.  
    · Press Psion-/ over the PAGESmgr icon to deinstall PAGESmgr from
      drive C, and unplug your Cyclone drive. Use Psion-i to install the 
      PAGESmgr and PAGESi icons on the System screen.  If this is the first
      time you have loaded Mobile Pages, simply press ‘Enter’ on the PAGESi 
      icons.  This will allow you to access, search and view the database(s)
      you have just downloaded.  If  you have loaded a new version of software
      or additional databases, simply enter PAGESmgr and select ‘Auto install’,
      before entering PAGESi.


   C) Installation procedure - Using RCOM or MCLINK
   ________________________________________________
     
     On the PC, start RCOM or MCLINK.   Insert the diskette into your PC's 
     diskette drive.  

     Copying the software - Copy the file pagesmgr.opa from your PC to
     any \app directory on your Psion and use Psion-i on the Psion to install
     the PAGESmgr program. Enter PAGESmgr on the Psion, answer a few simple
     questions, and the software will be copied to the Psion.

     Copying the database(s) - PAGESmgr will ask you if you want to load a 
     database from the PC.  Answering "Y" (for YES) will present you with a
     menu of databases available on the PC.  Select a database, answer a few
     simple questions, and the database will be copied to the Psion.  You 
     can repeat this step for every databases you want to download.  You can
     repeat it at any time in the future, by simply entering PAGESmgr and
     selecting the appropriate option.

     Exit PAGESmgr and use Psion-i to install PAGESi.opa on your Psion.  The 
     PAGESi icon will then appear on the screen.  Pressing 'Enter' on the PAGESi 
     icon will take you into 'Nicholson London Pages', allowing you to access,
     search and view the databases you have just downloaded.  
   
     You will see that with the software now fully loaded, if you re-enter 
     PAGESmgr, you will be presented with a new menu.  You will only need to
     use these options if, in the future, you want to download new software
     revisions and/or databases.  Such advanced use is documented in the file
     readme.2nd.


2) Creating your own Mobile Pages databases
___________________________________________
Demonstration versions of Pages Generator, the software tools used
to create Mobile Pages databases, are available from Mobile Software
and from our Web pages.  These tools are available, under a software
license agreement so that you can create your own Mobile Pages databases
with your own personal and/or business data. 


